{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"mental-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mental model"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Five ideas. Everything else in these docs is a consequence of one of them."}]},{"type":"component","name":"figure-mental-model","attributes":{},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-you-write-properties-not-classes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 · You write properties, not classes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A style is an object of CSS properties with real values. There is no vocabulary\nto memorise, no scale to look up before you can write a length, and no class-name\ngrammar to decode when you read it back."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"const card = css({\n  borderRadius: \"0.75rem\",\n  padding: \"1.5rem\",\n  boxShadow: \"0 1px 2px oklch(0 0 0 / 0.08)\",\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> card = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">borderRadius</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0.75rem&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">padding</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1.5rem&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">boxShadow</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0 1px 2px oklch(0 0 0 / 0.08)&quot;</span>,\n})"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Design tokens are ordinary imported values, so a token is just a constant your\neditor can show you; see "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tokens/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tokens"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-merging-replaces-entries-not-properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2 · Merging replaces entries, not properties"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the one that catches people, and it is worth ten minutes now rather than\nan afternoon later."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A property can hold several "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"entries"}]},{"type":"text","value":": one per condition. When you merge two\nstyles, the later one replaces "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the entries it names"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and leaves the rest alone."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"const base = css({\n  color: { base: \"black\", \":hover\": \"blue\" },\n})\n\n// Replaces the base entry. The `:hover` entry is still there.\nconst override = css({ color: \"grey\" })\n\n<a sx={[base, override]} /> // grey, and blue on hover","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> base = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">base</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;black&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;:hover&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;blue&quot;</span> },\n})\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// Replaces the base entry. The `:hover` entry is still there.</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">override</span> = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;grey&quot;</span> })\n\n&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">a</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={[base, <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">override</span>]} /&gt; <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// grey, and blue on hover</span>"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/merging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merging"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shows how to remove the entries you did not name."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-a-ladder-decides-what-wins-not-specificity","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3 · A ladder decides what wins, not specificity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every rule Kirana writes is one class, so every rule has the same specificity. A\nstated ladder decides instead, and two of its steps cover most days:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"More conditions win."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":":hover","source":":hover"}},{"type":"text","value":" value beats a base value."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then the narrower declaration."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"paddingTop","source":"paddingTop"}},{"type":"text","value":" beats "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"padding","source":"padding"}},{"type":"text","value":", in either order."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the ladder cannot separate two values, the compiler reports\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ambiguous-precedence","source":"ambiguous-precedence"}},{"type":"text","value":" instead of picking. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/precedence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Precedence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nis the whole ladder."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-style-what-you-render","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4 · Style what you render"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compiler styles elements it can see in your source. An element rendered inside\na component from an installed package is not yours, so "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" on that component does\nnothing unless the component reads it, and the compiler will tell you so\n("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx-on-external-component","source":"sx-on-external-component"}},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three ways out, in order of preference:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass compiled props, "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"{...<span class=\"th-token th-function\">props</span>(styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">thing</span>)}","source":"{...props(styles.thing)}"}},{"type":"text","value":", which works with any component\nthat spreads props onto an element."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Style it from an ancestor you do render, with\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/contextual","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"select","source":"select"}}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read its state from a parent with a "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/relations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"relation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-your-editor-shows-what-the-element-gets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 · Your editor shows what the element gets"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A class list puts the CSS on the element; a style object puts it behind a name. So\nthe language server writes it back where you read: every element's line ends with\nwhat it gets, in a class list's words."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"export function Plan({ featured }: { featured: boolean }) {\n  return (\n    <article sx={[card, featured && raised]}>\n      {\" \"}\n\n      <h2 sx={title}>Pro</h2>\n    </article>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"th-token th-function\">Plan</span>({ featured }: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">featured</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-type\">boolean</span> }) {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">return</span> (\n    &lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">article</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={[card, featured &amp;&amp; raised]}&gt;\n      {<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot; &quot;</span>}\n\n      &lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">h2</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={title}&gt;Pro&lt;/<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">h2</span>&gt;\n    &lt;/<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">article</span>&gt;\n  )\n}","variant":"editor","hints":"[{\"line\":4,\"text\":\"▦ grid · gap 1rem · p 1rem · featured: shadow lg\"},{\"line\":5,\"text\":\"text 1.25rem · 600 · ink\"}]","file":"src/plan.tsx","title":"src/plan.tsx"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read it the way you read "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"grid gap-<span class=\"th-token th-number\">4</span> p-<span class=\"th-token th-number\">4</span>","source":"grid gap-4 p-4"}},{"type":"text","value":". Hover it for the box model, every\ndeclaration with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"rem","source":"rem"}},{"type":"text","value":" in pixels and the token it reads, and the compiled rule;\nhover one property to see which entry wins and why. The answers come from the same\ncompiler session as the build, so the editor never disagrees with the stylesheet:\nif it shows "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"p <span class=\"th-token th-number\">1</span>rem","source":"p 1rem"}},{"type":"text","value":", the element gets "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"padding: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">1</span>rem","source":"padding: 1rem"}},{"type":"text","value":". See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"editor support"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"coming-from-somewhere-else","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Coming from somewhere else"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From Tailwind:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the vocabulary is the same ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@kirana-style/preset-scales","source":"@kirana-style/preset-scales"}},{"type":"text","value":" carries\nTailwind's scales), but conditions nest inside values instead of prefixing class\nnames, and the merge story is different from "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">cn</span>()","source":"cn()"}},{"type":"text","value":". The class list you read is\nstill there, at the end of the line in your editor (idea 5).\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/migration/from-tailwind","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From StyleX:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the API will look familiar. The difference that bites is idea\n2: StyleX's "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"default: null","source":"default: null"}},{"type":"text","value":" means \"no base value\", Kirana's "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"base: null","source":"base: null"}},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"removes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" an earlier one. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/migration/from-stylex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migration guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"mental-model","text":"Mental model","level":1},{"id":"1-you-write-properties-not-classes","text":"1 · You write properties, not classes","level":2},{"id":"2-merging-replaces-entries-not-properties","text":"2 · Merging replaces entries, not properties","level":2},{"id":"3-a-ladder-decides-what-wins-not-specificity","text":"3 · A ladder decides what wins, not specificity","level":2},{"id":"4-style-what-you-render","text":"4 · Style what you render","level":2},{"id":"5-your-editor-shows-what-the-element-gets","text":"5 · Your editor shows what the element gets","level":2},{"id":"coming-from-somewhere-else","text":"Coming from somewhere else","